PROPOSED AND ⛔ UNVALIDATED — make the swing-fighter sheet render REFUSE a
quality scale it cannot honour, instead of silently discarding it

    cd <repo root> && patch -p1 < dev/patches/swing-fighter-render-honours-quality-scale-20260902.patch

⛔ THE FILES ARE IN `tools/ambition_sprite2d_renderer`, A SUBMODULE. Applying
needs a commit there plus a pointer bump here. ⛔⛔ AND IT HAS NOT BEEN RUN: the
five touched files compile and the new helper's behaviour is exercised directly,
but no sheet has been rendered with it. Validate with one render on a box that
can run the renderer.

HOW YOU KNOW IT WORKED (one render each way, on a box that can run the renderer):

  1. THE DEFECT, now loud — this must FAIL with a ValueError naming the target,
     instead of writing a full-resolution sheet into a reduced tier directory:

       ambition_sprite2d_renderer publish --target medic \
           --quality-scale 0.25 --dest-root <...>/assets/sprites_0_25x

  2. THE ORDINARY PATH, unchanged — a publish with no `--quality-scale` (or 1.0)
     must render and install exactly as before. The guard returns early on
     `None` and on 1.0, so a normal regen must not notice this patch at all.
     `scripts/regen/sprites.sh --target medic` is the realistic form.

⚠ If (1) still succeeds, the helper is not reached — check that the target's
`render` calls it rather than opening with `del opts`. If (2) fails, the guard
is rejecting a scale it should pass through.

WHAT IT DOES. `performer`, `author`, `medic` and `officer` — the four targets
that import `_authored_swing_fighter.py`, and no others — each opened their
`render` with `del opts`. A caller that passed a scale:

    ambition_sprite2d_renderer publish --target medic \
        --quality-scale 0.25 --dest-root <...>/assets/sprites_0_25x

got a FULL-RESOLUTION sheet installed into a reduced tier, with nothing
indicating that anything had been ignored. Four sheets on one machine sat that
way for days — 67.2 MP where the tier promised ~10.5 — and nothing looked wrong
on screen, because the art is correct and merely larger than asked for.

⚠ IT DOES NOT IMPLEMENT SCALING, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. `render_portraits` in
the same class scales by shrinking its `output_size`; the sheet path has no
equivalent single knob. `frame_size()` is derived from
`doc.frame["render_scale"]` while the frames themselves come from `_raw_frame`,
so scaling `frame_size` alone would shrink the LAYOUT and not the art —
cropping every frame at its new edge. **That is the one failure Jon's standing
rule forbids, and it would look like a successful render.** Implementing real
scaling needs a rasterisation review by someone who can run the renderer;
making the discard loud does not, and removes the silence that let this sit.

ⓘ AND THE TIERS DO NOT NEED THIS PATH. `generate_visual_quality_variants.py`
sends every `module`-kind target — which is all four of these — to
`build_sheet_variant`, which RESIZES the published full sheet from isolated
frames. That is the road every correctly-scaled variant already comes from, and
it is why a fresh-clone generation produces correct tiers for all four while a
box that ran the per-tier CLI does not. After this patch, that CLI invocation
fails loudly instead of publishing full-size art into a tier directory.

⇒ Companion reading: the reconciliation paragraph in
`docs/planning/engine/asset-preparation-and-residency.md` (Open work 5), which
names which road produces which tier file and why two boxes disagreed.

